1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:04,780
是的 我保证一拿到结果就给你打电话
Yes, I promise I'll call you as soon as I get the results.

2
00:00:05,300 --> 00:00:08,640
是的 我知道医院是滋生传染病的温床
Yes, I am aware that hospitals are a hotbed of infection.

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:09,855
谢你了 曼尼
Thank you, Manny.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,080
几周前 我的心脏出了一点小状况
A couple of weeks ago, I had a minor heart incident.

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,120
我好得很
I am fine.

6
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,340
但为了安全考虑 我要去做个血管造影
But just to be safe, I'm having an angiogram,

7
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:17,060
也就是说他们会输入一种染色剂
which is when they inject a dye

8
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:18,440
以确保没有栓塞
to make sure there's no blockage.

9
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:20,140
不是什么大事
It's--it's no big deal.

10
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:21,380
-我们毫不担心 -不担心
- We're not worried. - No.

11
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:24,440
如果真出了什么事 虽然肯定不会
If something were to happen, which it's not...

12
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:25,040
不会出事的
Not gonna.

13
00:00:25,620 --> 00:00:28,320
我会把我们的卧室改造成供奉克莱尔的灵堂
I would turn our bedroom into a shrine to Claire.

14
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,480
把这间房改造成魔术大厅
And this room into a hall of magic.

15
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:35,880
卢克 别再拆小家电了
Luke, please stop taking appliances apart.

16
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:38,020
-我在做东西 -你在毁东西
- I'm making something. - You're unmaking something.

17
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:40,340
-因为我今天要递交辞呈 -等等 什么
- 'cause I'm giving my notice today. - Wait. What?

18
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:42,820
我们难道不喜欢已经抹上黄油的烤面包吗
But wouldn't we rather have toast that's already buttered?

19
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:45,171
我就爱你问这种稀奇古怪的问题
I love that you're asking these kind of questions.

20
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:47,340
如果弹簧能够更强力一点
If only the springs were stronger,

21
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:49,920
面包片就可以被发射到黄油罐中
the toast would be catapulted into the pool of butter.

22
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:51,140
超强力的弹簧
Really strong springs,

23
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:52,400
比如你床垫里的那种吗
like the ones in your mattress?

24
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:54,500
你真是一语惊醒梦中人
You're unbelievable.

25
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:56,340
什么叫你不干了
What do you mean you're quitting?

26
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:58,200
你们经理刚让你负责
Your manager just started letting you

27
00:00:58,200 --> 00:00:59,480
早上开门和晚上关门
open and close the store.

28
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:00,560
那太无聊了
It's boring.

29
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:03,040
珍妮弗说我可以在珠宝店得到一份工作
And Jennifer said that I could get a job at the jewelry store.

30
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:04,820
宝贝 你必须学会持之以恒
Honey, you need to learn to stick with things.

31
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:07,020
你刚把钥匙拿到手
You just got the big keys.

32
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:07,973
咖啡壶哪儿去了
Where's the coffeepot?

33
00:01:07,973 --> 00:01:10,020
你是说即将改造完成的咖啡机器人吗
Oh, you mean the soon-to-be coffee bot?

34
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:11,420
-卢克 -我今天需要咖啡因提神
- Luke! - I need caffeine today.

35
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:12,560
你可以喝果汁
You can have juice.

36
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:14,400
你昨晚在那个派对玩到多晚
How late were you at that party last night?

37
00:01:14,888 --> 00:01:16,540
拜托 她10点就溜回家了
Oh, please. She snuck in at 10:00

38
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:19,060
然后整晚都用手电筒躲在被子里读书
And spent all night reading under the covers with a flashlight.

39
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:20,380
艾丽克斯 我不是说让你
Alex, what have I told you

40
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,720
要在宵禁时间之后再回家吗
about staying out past your curfew?

41
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:24,060
-我需要再多玩几次 -对极了
- I need to do it more often. - Exactly.

42
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,140
你得学会享受乐趣
You need to learn to have some fun.

43
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:29,660
你要和妮可一起参加春假旅游
You are going on that spring break trip with Nicole.

44
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:30,960
不 不行 我不能去
No! No, I can't.

45
00:01:30,960 --> 00:01:32,562
我得为高考预考做准备
I have to study for the P.S.A.T.S.

46
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:35,220
卢克 菲尔 快教育一下你的孩子们
Luke! Phil, talk to your children.

47
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:36,980
好吧 大家都给我听好了
All right. Everybody listen up.

48
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,080
海莉 你不能说不干了
Haley, you're not quitting.

49
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:39,940
你要说辞职 那好听一点
You're resigning. It sounds better.

50
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,540
-不对 -艾丽克斯 你可以把整个春假
- No. - Alex, you have all of spring break

51
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:44,380
都用来将自己锁在屋子里看书
to lock yourself in your room and study.

52
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:45,040
不 不 不 不对
No, no, no, no, no.

53
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:47,500
卢克 咖啡机器人是不可能成功的
And, Luke, coffee bot is a non-starter.

54
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:48,780
但我很喜欢你提出
But I do like the idea

55
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:50,700
把玉米粒放进煎饼面糊里
of popcorn kernels in the pancake batter...

56
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:51,660
那样它们就可以自动翻边了
So they self-flip.

57
00:01:51,660 --> 00:01:52,620
别说了
Stop talking!

58
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,160
离我的孩子们远些
Step away from the children.

59
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:18,287
曼尼
Manny?

60
00:02:18,928 --> 00:02:20,680
我在夸你长得帅
I am telling you how handsome you are.

61
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:22,100
下次直接用英语说好了
Oh. Well, next time, tell me in English

62
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:22,780
那样我就不会错过了
So I don't miss it.

63
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:25,140
你的西班牙语都快忘光了 你从来不练习
You're forgetting all your Spanish. You never practice.

64
00:02:25,140 --> 00:02:28,280
"原谅我 妈咪 我有了"
Perdoname, mami, soy embarazada.

65
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:31,054
你刚是在说你怀孕了
You just told me that you're pregnant.

66
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,620
恭喜呀 你散发着母性的光辉
Congratulations. You're glowing.

67
00:02:32,940 --> 00:02:34,280
不是吧 你就穿成这样
Really? That's what you're wearing?

68
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,220
不是吧 你对你的"饭票"这么无礼
Really? That's how you talk to your meal ticket?

69
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,540
再说 那些势利眼也不会在乎我穿什么
Besides, those snobs don't care what I wear,

70
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:40,240
只要我带上支票簿就行
as long as I bring my checkbook.

71
00:02:40,507 --> 00:02:43,200
今天我要去德莱顿学院进行一场面试
Today I have an interview with the Dryden academy.

72
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,460
那是附近最有威望的预科学校
It's only the most prestigious prep school around.

73
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:47,740
他们的校歌有36句诗
Their school song has 36 verses,

74
00:02:47,740 --> 00:02:49,100
我全都掌握了
and I know all of 'em.

75
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,780
准备好
Settle in.

76
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:53,920
为什么你不带他去
And the reason you're not bringing him?

77
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:56,020
他说我让他紧张
He says that I make him nervous,

78
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:57,320
说我关心则乱
that I care too much.

79
00:02:57,380 --> 00:03:00,380
现在我都不能带他去理发了
That's why I'm not even allowed to bring him to his haircuts anymore.

80
00:03:01,460 --> 00:03:03,320
我从没上过私立学校
I never went to private school.

81
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:05,580
我甚至大学都没读完
Hell, I never even finished college,

82
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:08,380
但你瞧瞧我 我刚吃的丹麦糕点要6美元
And look at me. That danish I just ate cost 6 bucks.

83
00:03:08,620 --> 00:03:09,440
我都没眨一下眼
I didn't even blink.

84
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:12,080
我一直觉得在公立学校格格不入
I've always felt out of place in public school,

85
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:14,540
就像洋葱地里开出的一朵矮牵牛花
like a lone petunia in an onion patch.

86
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,220
你觉得格格不入
You felt out of place?

87
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,860
我来让你了解一下预科学校的学生们吧
Let me tell you something about your prep school buddies.

88
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,740
我年轻的时候 曾干过一份工作
When I was younger, I had a job

89
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:23,680
是在乡村俱乐部帮人挂衣帽
checking coats at a country club.

90
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:26,060
那些自大的富二代得意地走进去
These smug rich kids used to waltz in there

91
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:28,120
直接把大衣扔到我身上 就像我是奴隶一样
and throw their coats at me like I was nothing.

92
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:30,260
那时候高级面料还没有诞生
That was before your high-tech fabrics.

93
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:30,940
那些大衣重死了
They weighed a ton.

94
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:32,440
你看到这个疤痕了吗
You see that scar?

95
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:33,640
那不是你在战场留下的吗
The one you got in the war?

96
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:34,920
那是我对外人的说法
That's what I tell people.

97
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:39,840
我被一件巴宝莉粗呢大衣的棒形纽扣击中了
I caught the scalloped edge of a burberry duffel coat toggle.

98
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:43,740
我现在也不确定有没有残片留在里面
Still not sure there isn't a piece in there.

99
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:47,960
如果你允许 孩子们总会
Kids will always want to quit

100
00:03:47,969 --> 00:03:49,598
在遇到困难的时候就不想干了
when things get hard if you let 'em.

101
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:52,380
那姑娘可是被大学赶出来了
This is a girl who was kicked out of college.

102
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,840
她好歹也该再坚持坚持
The least she can do is stick it out at a little--

103
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:55,740
-菲尔 -抱歉
- Phil? - Sorry.

104
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:58,100
听着 我们应该给海莉一些时间
Look, all we can do is give Haley the time

105
00:03:58,100 --> 00:03:59,140
让她认清自己
to find out who she is.

106
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,200
或者我们省下那点时间
Or we could save that time,

107
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,360
我直接告诉她她是怎样的一个人
and I could tell her who she is.

108
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:02,920
一定要记得告诉我结果如何
Let me know how that works out.

109
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:04,080
你说什么
Excuse me?

110
00:04:04,620 --> 00:04:06,580
抱歉 我的电视坏了
Oh, sorry, but my TV doesn't work,

111
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:07,760
我只能观赏你们的好戏了
and you're all I've got.

112
00:04:07,760 --> 00:04:09,660
-我叫诺曼 -很高兴见到你 诺曼
- I'm Norman. - Good to meet you, Norman.

113
00:04:09,780 --> 00:04:10,600
你是因为什么入院的
What are you in for?

114
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:11,940
-做冠脉搭桥手术 -太好了
- Triple bypass. - Awesome.

115
00:04:12,180 --> 00:04:14,440
你似乎很赞同我教育子女的方法嘛
And it sounded like you were agreeing with my parenting style,

116
00:04:14,440 --> 00:04:15,900
所以请您老继续说吧
So, please, continue.

117
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,880
我养了三个孩子
Well, I've raised three kids,

118
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:19,260
我学到的最重要一点
and the main thing I learned is

119
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:21,520
就是让他们保持真我
you have to let them be who they are.

120
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:22,580
谢谢你 诺曼
Thank you, Norman.

121
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:25,280
虽然他在幕布后面 并不代表他是巫师
Just because he's behind a curtain doesn't make him a wizard.

122
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:28,200
爸 我给你做了这个项链
Dad, I made you this necklace.

123
00:04:28,260 --> 00:04:29,080
有助于疾病痊愈
It's good for healing.

124
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:31,260
那毫无科学依据 爸
There's no scientific evidence to back that up, dad.

125
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:33,300
-我老公是个医生 -我有三个学位
- I married a doctor. - I have three degrees.

126
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:34,780
女儿们 你们的小弟呢
Girls, where's your little brother?

127
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:37,940
他没把胳膊卡在自动贩卖机里吧
He didn't get his arm stuck In a vending machine again, did he?

128
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,900
你看出来了吗
Are you getting this?

129
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:42,200
是的 听上去就跟我们家孩子一样
Yes. They sound just like our kids,

130
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,000
他们都一起来探望父亲
And they all got together to visit their dad...

131
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:46,240
他显然把儿女教育得很成功
who apparently did a pretty good job raising them.

132
00:04:46,420 --> 00:04:47,640
得了吧 他听上去就跟老嬉皮士一样
Please. He sounds like an old hippie.

133
00:04:47,940 --> 00:04:49,640
一个睿智 富有洞察力的老嬉皮
A wise, insightful, old hippie.

134
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:50,760
像大明星杰夫·布里奇斯那样的嬉皮
A Jeff Bridges hippie.

135
00:04:51,080 --> 00:04:52,580
-爸 -宝贝儿子来了
- Hey, dad. - There he is!

136
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,420
瞧那身笔挺的西装
Look at that sharp suit.

137
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:56,700
天啊 卢克变得好威武雄壮
Oh, my god, Luke gets huge.

138
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:57,520
你见过啊
You've seen this.

139
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:58,520
我穿过这身去参加安琪拉的婚礼
I wore it to Angela's wedding.

140
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:01,940
是啊 就跟我为小乔纳森做的那件一样
Yeah. It's just like the one I had made for my little jonathan.

141
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:03,380
好了 邓菲太太
Okay, Mrs. Dunphy.

142
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,500
-你该做术前准备了 -好吧
- Time for your prep. - Okay.

143
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:08,000
你瞧见父母如果不干预孩子的发展会怎样吧
See what happens when parents get out of the way?

144
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,800
婚礼 宝宝 笔挺的西装
Weddings, babies, sharp suits.

145
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,940
你可能得推她去烧伤病房
You might want to wheel her by the burn unit.

146
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:13,980
她的信心刚刚被灼伤了
She just got scorched.

147
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:17,460
慢着 你给乔纳森做了一套西装
Wait. You made a suit for Jonathan?

148
00:05:17,900 --> 00:05:18,880
他是只猫啊
He's a cat.

149
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:21,920
他是只无毛流浪猫 需要西装保暖
He's a hairless stray. He needs the suit for warmth.

150
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:22,820
你懂那种感觉的
You know, that thing.

151
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:24,980
每一任丈夫最后都抛弃了你
All of your husbands eventually stop feeling for you.

152
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:26,480
我不是来被你羞辱的
I did not come here to be insulted.

153
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,960
我是来看望老爸的
I came here for dad.

154
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,480
老爸 我需要500块
Dad, I need $500.

155
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:33,540
你怎么会缺钱 你有四份离婚协议书啊
How can you need money? You have four divorce settlements.

156
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:36,500
对 抱歉我不是空虚寂寞冷的驱魔人
Yeah, sorry I'm not some sad, lonely exorcist.

157
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:38,640
是档案管理员 我是档案管理员
Archivist. I'm an archivist.

158
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:40,380
拜托 吵死了
Ugh. This arguing.

159
00:05:40,380 --> 00:05:42,260
我还不如在法庭待着
I might as well have just stayed in court.

160
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:43,840
一定要是名律师 一定要是名律师
Please be a lawyer. Please be a lawyer.

161
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:44,500
结果怎样
How'd it go?

162
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:47,320
-缓刑期 可以释放 -行啊你
- I got probation plus time served. - Suck it!

163
00:05:47,461 --> 00:05:49,120
看来你不会再用肉钩
Well, maybe now you'll stop

164
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:51,280
从电网偷电了哟
siphoning electricity off the grid with a meat hook.

165
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,580
嘿 看着我
Hey, look at me for a second.

166
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:54,780
当你在床上孤独地死去
When you die alone in your bed,

167
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,280
乔纳森会啃光你的肉
Jonathan's going to eat you.

168
00:05:58,227 --> 00:05:59,185
没错
Yep.

169
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:03,980
莉莉 闺蜜日开始咯
